leave_policies = """Leave Policy
1.1. Purpose of the Leave Policy
To provide employees with time away from their job for rest, relaxation and personal pursuits and to facilitate a culture of work-life balance.
1.2. Annual Leave Entitlement
All full-time regular employees are entitled to leaves up to a pre-determined limit:
Confirmed Employees: 16 days per annum
Confirmed Employees are entitled to 16 days of leave per annum, credited quarterly at 4 days per quarter.
Trainees/Consultants: 1 day per month
Trainees/Consultants are entitled to 1 day of leave per month. The leave must be utilized within the same month and is not eligible for carry forward to the subsequent month.
1.3. Leave Break-up
Medical / Emergency Leaves- 8 Days per annum
Employees are entitled to eight days of Medical/Emergency Leave per annum, which may be availed strictly in cases of genuine medical or unforeseen emergencies. The employee is required to inform their immediate reporting manager at the earliest possible time in such circumstances. The leave application must be applied through the ERP system on the very next working day an individual join back to work. Any Medical/Emergency Leave availed in excess to the annual entitlement of eight days will be considered as LWP.
Note- Medical certificate or doctor prescription will be required in case leave exceeds more then 4 days
Casual / Earned Leaves - 8 Days per annum
Employees are entitled to eight days of Casual Leave per annum. Casual Leave must be applied through the ERP system at least two (2) days in advance for approval. If an employee proceeds on Casual Leave without prior approval, such leave will be treated as Loss of Pay (LWP) and salary will be deducted at 1.5x of leave days taken.
No Casual Leave will be approved if it is applied after the leave has already been consumed. Any Casual / Earned Leave availed in excess to the annual entitlement of eight days will be considered as LWP.
Unapproved Leave / No Leave Balance
Any leave that is unapproved, taken when the employee has zero leave balance, or not applied through ERP, irrespective of the leave category, will be treated as Loss of Pay (LWP).
In such cases, salary will be deducted at 1.5x of leave days taken.
If an employee has no leave balance, any additional approved leave will be treated as Leave Without Pay (LWP), and salary will be deducted at 1x of the leave days taken.
Company Holidays – 10 Days
Besides Medical & leave every year our company observes ten days as official company holidays on account of National holidays/festivals. The specific dates for each year are declared annually, at the beginning of each year in accordance with the Government of India Holidays.
Compensatory Leave
In case employees are required to work on a holiday, they are eligible for compensatory leave. An employee will be eligible for a compensatory leave only if he/she has worked 8 hours on the holiday. Compensatory leave will be provided at the discretion of the respective Team Lead. Employee is required to send request for the same on ERP and need to take approval from Lead/PM within a week of the day worked on. It is compulsory to use some tracker (Hub staff/Upwork/or any other as decided by company from time to time) and provide the details via ERP.
Short leave
Employees can take one short leave(0.25) in a month and this will be deducted from the Employee's leave balance.
1.4. Leave Calculation Process
All leave entitlements are determined for the calendar year i.e. from 1st Jan. to 31st Dec.
Leaves are credited quarterly basis and are calculated on a pro-rata basis base on DOJ and when someone is on resignation.
Members joining or leaving anytime in-between the year would get their leave calculated on pro-rata basis. Members who terminate their employment with the Company and have used leave in excess of their entitlement will be required to repay the Company amounts in excess (if any).
Sandwich Policy:
Any leaves applied on working days and combined with a holiday and a weekend results in treating the weekend as leaves.
5+2 Rule: In case leave is taken for entire workweek then weekend at end of leaves will also be counted as leaves.
One weekend in a year per employee will be waived off from the sandwich policy. The waiver is available for the confirmed employees only.
If an employee attends the office for only one day in a week and remains absent for the rest of the working days, the entire week may be treated as sandwich leave, subject to the reporting manager’s approval.
Example 1 Leave Combined with Holiday + Weekend (Sandwich Rule)
In 2026, Republic Dayfalls on Monday, 26 January 2026.
If an employee applies for leave on: Friday, 23 January 2026 & Tuesday, 27 January 2026- Total leaves counted: 4 days
Example 2 5+2 Rule (Entire Workweek Leave)
As per the 5+2 rule, when the entire workweek is taken as leave, the following weekend is also counted
If an employee applies for leave from: Monday, 13 April 2026 to Friday, 17 April 2026- Total leaves counted: 7 days
Example 3 Weekend + Public Holiday (One-Sided Sandwich)
Leave Before Weekend + Public Holiday
In 2026, Republic Day falls on Monday, 26 January 2026.
If an employee applies for leave on: Friday, 23 January 2026 - Total leaves counted: 3 days
Leave After Weekend + Public Holiday
In 2026, Republic Day falls on Monday, 26 January 2026.
If an employee applies for leave on: Tuesday, 27 January 2026 - Total leaves counted: 3 days
1.5. Leave during Probation
If an employee leaves the Company during the three-month probation period, any leave availed during this period shall be deducted from the final settlement. Leave availed during probation is neither eligible for encashment nor adjustable against the notice period.
For the purpose of this policy, completion of the probation period is defined as ninety (90) days. Employment shall be considered confirmed only upon receiving of an official confirmation email from the Company. In the absence of such communication, the probation period shall be deemed to be extended. Leave days taken during the probation period shall not be counted toward the completion of the probation period.
1.6. For Members on Training
Leave entitlement is one leave per month during training period.
Leave cannot be carried forward.
Leave cannot be en-cashed.
Any extra leaves taken will result in the date of confirmation as employee being extended by same
1.7. Leave Application Process
Approval for leave is taken through ERP ONLY.
The Immediate Supervisor/Manager recommends leave.
Leave equal to or more than four days requires the Director’s/ Founder’s approval or PM/TL who are directly reporting to Upper Management.
For all leaves, employees should send request via ERP and can proceed with leaves after approval.
Under exceptional circumstances (i.e., sickness or urgent work) if the member is not able to apply for leave beforehand he/she must inform their respective Managers/Supervisor as soon as possible and should apply via ERP on the day he/she returns from leave.
If absent without Leave sanction/ approval or beyond eligibility, the absence would be considered as Leave without Pay (LWP).
Employees are required to adhere to office timings i.e. entry between 9:00 am to 10:00 am and complete 8 office hours every day. In absence of non-completion of work hours & office hours leaves will be deducted as applicable.
It is the responsibility of each member to maintain his/her individual account of leave and plan leaves keeping in view the work requirements.
1.8. Maternity Leave
Confirmed female employees will be eligible for Maternity Leave as per Maternity Benefit Act 1961 and Maternity-Benefit-Act- NOTIFICATION-29.03.2017
Note: This benefit is not available to employees on probation
1.9. Leave Encashment Policy
Unutilized leave, up to a maximum of nine (9) days, shall be eligible for encashment at the end of the calendar year, i.e., in the month of December or at the time of separation, whichever is earlier.
Leave encashment will be calculated based on the basic salary drawn. In case of increment during the calendar year, leave encashment will be calculated on a pro-rata basis.
Though the Company encourages employees to exhaust their annual leave entitlements each year and promotes taking time off in preference to leave payouts.
1.10. Weekly Minimum Work Hours Compliance
All employees are required to complete a minimum of 16 working hours per week, irrespective of leave utilization.
Failure to complete 16 working hours in any given week, without approved leave or authorized justification, may result in salary deduction on a pro-rata basis, including deduction of applicable weekend days."""